---
// The VCF 9 model at a glance: fleet, instances, domains. Same content as the diagram in the note
// "The VCF 9 mental model". Real text in CSS blocks rather than an SVG, so it reflows on a phone and stays
// at reading size. In each instance the workload domains stack beside the management domain, so a domain
// with only a name is a short block rather than an empty box.
---
<figure class="fleet">
  <figcaption>VCF 9 puts a fleet and instances above the domains you knew from 5.x. <a href="/vcf/library/architecture/vcf9-mental-model/">Read the note</a></figcaption>
  <div class="fleet-draw">
    <span class="fleet-l">Fleet</span>
    <div class="fleet-top"><b>VCF Operations · VCF Automation</b><span>Console, licensing, identity and fleet lifecycle</span></div>
    <div class="fleet-insts">
      <div class="fleet-inst">
        <span class="fleet-l">Instance 1</span>
        <div class="fleet-doms">
          <div class="fleet-dom m"><b>Management domain</b>SDDC Manager<br />vCenter · NSX<br />Services runtime</div>
          <div class="fleet-dom"><b>Workload domain</b>vCenter · NSX</div>
          <div class="fleet-dom"><b>Workload domain</b></div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="fleet-inst i2">
        <span class="fleet-l">Instance 2</span>
        <div class="fleet-doms">
          <div class="fleet-dom m"><b>Management domain</b>SDDC Manager<br />vCenter · NSX<br />Services runtime</div>
          <div class="fleet-dom"><b>Workload domains</b>One vCenter each,<br />NSX own or shared</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</figure>
